 "why_this_exists": [
  "The F-clef dot veto had no corpus. Every change to it was being judged on",
  "coverage and on three corpora that contain no bass clef the locator is",
  "liable to call a C clef \u2014 so the COST of a veto change was measurable and",
  "its BENEFIT was an anecdote. That is the trade this layer refuses, and it",
  "is why the held-back clustering (ClefLocatorConfig.cluster_y_gap_spaces)",
  "and every threshold change stalled: the harnesses could not see the thing",
  "they were being held back for.",
  "",
  "Method: run the locator with clustering ON over pages 2-80 of the score,",
  "take every staff it LOCATES a C clef on, render the header crop, and read",
  "the glyph by eye. 101 located reads; 92 not already in the spot check.",
  "",
  "Seventeen of them are bass clefs and seven are treble clefs. Those are the",
  "twenty-four the veto exists to catch, and none of them appeared in any",
  "corpus before this file. The rest are genuine C clefs and are here as the",
  "counterweight: a veto that fires on everything would score perfectly",
  "without them.",
  "",
  "One staff was excluded rather than guessed at (p66 s10, crop too tight to",
  "read). Reading a glyph wrong here is worse than omitting it.",
  "",
  "Every 'mezzosoprano' read in the sweep was a misread G clef \u2014 7 of 7. That",
  "is a pattern worth its own look, and it is recorded here rather than acted",
  "on."
 ],
